# Side panels made after the view mode was applied follow it (client/BASE.md 0077; owner debug item 1: "Show right horizontal panel + resize do mapa: a black bar"). refreshViewMode paints every side panel 'white' (classic view) or 'alpha' (extended view: the map is the full-screen background, the panels float over it) and the two horizontal panels the same. The minimap expansion's spacer panel (reserveMinimapExpansionSpace, made when the minimap is widened), a panel added with addRightPanel / addLeftPanel and the horizontal panels shown later kept the default white image: an opaque near-black frame (12,10,14) over the map. Now each is painted by applySidePanelColor when made or shown. Lua only. Applies after 0001-0076.
--- a/modules/game_interface/gameinterface.lua
+++ b/modules/game_interface/gameinterface.lua
@@ -49,6 +49,16 @@
   return panel and panel.minimapExpansionReservation == true
 end
 
+-- refreshViewMode paints every side panel 'white' (classic view) or 'alpha' (extended view: the map is the full-screen
+-- background and the panels float over it). A panel or spacer made later has to follow, or it is an opaque near-black
+-- bar over the map (the "black bar" with the right horizontal panel shown and the minimap expanded: the expansion's
+-- spacer panel was created white and covered the map).
+local function applySidePanelColor(panel)
+  if panel then
+    panel:setImageColor(isClassicViewActive() and 'white' or 'alpha')
+  end
+end
+
 -- The reservation stands in for the space the expanded minimap covers, so it has to stay
